    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.operators\n\n### Description\n\ncan't use `\"%` `\".` `\":` registers with `gr` operator\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\npress `\"%grr` and an error occurs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua Vim:E354: Invalid register name: '%'\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'setreg'\r\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/operators.lua:1033: in function 'replace_do'\r\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/operators.lua:483: in function <.../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/operators.lua:460>\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nreplace current line with file name\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nerror",
